{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Even not to a land. And you have given us.</b> It is not enough that you did us harm to bring us out of a land flowing with milk and honey into the wilderness — you also mock us, in that you have not brought us to the land you spoke of at all. Your words are as though you had given us an inheritance of field and vineyard in it, by commanding us commandments that depend on the land and saying ״לֹא תְכַלֶּה פְּאַת שָׂדְךָ וּפֶרֶט כַּרְמְךָ״ (Leviticus 19:9–10), as though it were already ours and we had in it field and vineyard." "<b>Will you gouge out the eyes of those men?</b> Do you intend to gouge out our eyes so that we will not recognize your stratagems?"], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:40:09.412703099Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}